# Stenion dashboard configuration.
#
# As of the Vercel deploy merge (2026-08-12) the dashboard is the ONE deployable:
# it hosts its own API routes (app/api/protocols, app/api/protocol/[id]) and the
# cron-trigger route (app/api/cron/run-indexer) in-process. It therefore reads the
# database + on-chain endpoints DIRECTLY — there is no separate API service and no
# STENION_API_URL any more (that variable is removed; delete it if present).
#
# LOCAL DEV: you do NOT normally need a dashboard/.env.local. The db/indexer code
# walks up from the current directory to find the repo-root .env, so DATABASE_URL,
# STENION_RPC_URL, STENION_HORIZON_URL and CRON_SECRET are all inherited from the
# single repo-root .env (see ../.env.example). Only create a .env.local here to
# override one of those for the dashboard specifically.
#
# ON VERCEL: set these in the project's Environment Variables (see ../.env.example
# "Deploying to Vercel"):
#   DATABASE_URL         — Neon pooled connection string (used by the API routes AND
#                          the server-rendered pages, which read the Store in-process)
#   STENION_RPC_URL      — Soroban RPC        (cron route only)
#   STENION_HORIZON_URL  — Horizon            (cron route only)
#   CRON_SECRET          — shared secret for POST /api/cron/run-indexer
